[KiCad-IOS port] Round 23: fix Round 22's own crash -- the
uninitialized m_preview3DCanvas -- and instrument the chooser
frame with stage breadcrumbs.

Diagnosis (hidden_files/round23-bug-ledger.md #1,
SOURCE-CONVICTED and verified three times): Sean device-tested
the Round 22 build (v0.8) and the footprint library button
STILL crashed the app, from Symbol Properties. Round 22 patch
0051 removed the chooser's desktop-OpenGL EDA_3D_CANVAS on iOS
by compiling out the assignment in build3DCanvas(), and its
header asserts "m_preview3DCanvas stays null". It does not:
EDA_3D_CANVAS* m_preview3DCanvas (footprint_chooser_frame.h)
has NO in-class initializer, and the constructor's initializer
list does not mention it. Upstream never noticed because
build3DCanvas() assigned it unconditionally before any read.
On iOS the sole writer is compiled out, no patch in the series
ever writes nullptr to it, and the member is INDETERMINATE.
Every guard 0051 added -- the constructor's guarded Show right
after build3DCanvas() returns, updatePanelsVisibility() /
updateViews() later in the same constructor, the destructor's
guarded teardown -- tests garbage. The frame is heap-allocated
with plain new (pcbnew.cpp) inside a long session full of
freed dialog allocations, so the slot in practice holds a
stale non-null pointer and the first guarded Show() dispatches
virtually through it: EXC_BAD_ACCESS inside Player(), before
KiwayMailIn and before ShowModal, on the exact click Sean
reported. (Both of patch 0052's sites are safe: upstream
initialises m_previewPane and m_modelViewer to nullptr in
their init lists. The chooser was the only one of the three
whose "stays null" claim was never made true.)

Fix (pcbnew/footprint_chooser_frame.h): give the member the
in-class null initialiser, `= nullptr`. Unconditional (it is a
no-op on desktop, where build3DCanvas() still assigns before
any read) and impossible to preprocess out -- the Round 22
attempt-1 failure mode cannot recur for this fix.

Instrumentation (pcbnew/footprint_chooser_frame.cpp, all under
KICAD_IOS_PORT, via PATHS::IosBreadcrumb from patch 0054):
stage markers bracket every remaining suspect stage of the
chooser's construction and display -- 10-ctor-enter,
11-panel-done, 12-canvas-aliased, 13-3d-skipped (inside
build3DCanvas, next to the Round 22 trace; its comment there
now also corrects the false "stays null" claim),
14-3dguard-passed (immediately after the guarded Show that
faulted: 13-present/14-absent in the device log re-convicts
this span on any future build; 14-present clears it),
15-tools-done, 16-frame-ready, 17-mailin-enter,
18-mailin-exit, 19-showmodal-override, 20-dtor-enter,
21-dtor-3d-done. If the crash persists despite the fix, the
last line of Documents/kicad-ios-breadcrumb.log names the
dying stage instead of another round of guessing.

